  "final_text": "The September invoice fills the one gap in the 2025 data. It changes **F2** and **F3**. **F4** stays the same.\n\n**What the photo shows.** Invoice EL-25-09 covers 01–30.09.2025 and bills 41,200 kWh at 9.50 MKD/kWh, which comes to 391,400 MKD. The meter readings agree: 1,325,550 − 1,284,350 = 41,200 kWh.\n\n**A problem in the CSV.** October (EL-25-10) is in there twice, once as the e-invoice and once as a scan. It must be counted only once. If you count it twice and leave out September, you get 318.4 MWh. That looks believable but is wrong.\n\n| Field | Before (Sep missing, Oct once) | With September |\n|---|---|---|\n| **F2** Electricity use 2025 | 279.7 MWh (only 11 months, not a full year) | **320.9 MWh** (measured, from 12 invoices) |\n| **F3** PV yield and share | 180 MWh ≈ 64% | **180 MWh ≈ 56%** of consumption *(estimate: the installer's yield, not measured)* |\n| **F4** Simple payback | 8,550,000 / (180,000 × 9.50) = 5.0 years | **5.0 years, unchanged** *(estimate, based on the installer's yield)* |\n\nF4 doesn't change because the bank's formula uses only the investment, the expected yield and the price. Consumption isn't part of it.\n\n**Before you submit:**\n- The photo is stamped **КОПИЈА** (copy), and September isn't booked in the invoice list. Ask the supplier for the e-invoice or the original and book it, so the bank can trace F2 back to your records.\n- The October scan is a duplicate of the e-invoice. Check that it wasn't booked or paid twice.\n- The solar offer is dated 2 September 2026 and is valid for 60 days, so it **expires around 1 November 2026**. It's also unsigned. If the bank's review will run past that date, ask the installer to extend it.\n- These files contain nothing for F1, F5 or F6 (fines, employees and accidents, certificates). Those fields still need their own sources.",
